B8 — THE COURT'S LAST REDOUBT + S921's EMPTY MUTANT
========================================================================
  The court itself handed back the frame: "agreement with the textbook = a
  frame, multiplicity 0" — and fell back to ONE claim: "the load-bearing new
  measurement = ZERO linear invariants". Question: is this last redoubt a
  separate fact, or the same one?


  ⟹ η is a bijection between invariant VECTORS and invariant
     COVECTORS. "Zero linear invariants" ≡ "there is no invariant
     vector" — and that is a one-line corollary of irreducibility (a fixed
     vector spans a 1-dimensional trivial sub-representation; irreducibility +
     n≥2 ⟹ it is zero).

  ⇒ ★★THE LAST REDOUBT FALLS. The claim the court PULLED OUT from under the frame as "a load-bearing NEW measurement" is the very same textbook fact, reached by η-conjugation from what the court itself marked with multiplicity 0. The multiplicity of A2 = 0 IN FULL, including the exception the court kept for itself.

  ★AS A SIDE EFFECT — S921's mutant m3 IS EMPTY (class: a mutant that could not survive):

  ⇒ ★S921's m3 = "there exists a SECOND independent invariant symmetric form". But dim=1 in EVERY signature n=3..7 without exception ⟹ this mutant could not have survived ANYWHERE. A mutant that cannot fail to be caught measures nothing — it is not a kill-test, but a tautology. ⟹ "mutants 3/3 CAUGHT ⟹ the measurement is valid" in S921 should be read as 2/3 (m1, m2 are real). Not a wrong number — a wrong IMPLICATION, exactly the class [[zero-from-a-count-that-never-ran]].

